==English==
[[File:M0354_1951-38-021_1.jpg|thumb|pince-nez]]

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|pince-nez|lit=pinch-nose}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/pænsˈneɪ/|/pæ̃sˈneɪ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pince-nez.wav|Audio (UK)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|pince-nez}}

# [[temple]]-less [[eyeglasses]] that [[clip]] to the [[bridge]] of the nose
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1919|author={{w|P. G. Wodehouse}}|title={{w|A Damsel in Distress (novel)|A Damsel in Distress}}|chapter=15| passage=Lord Belpher, leaning against the wall and trying to decide whether his right or left foot hurt him the more excruciatingly, became aware that a curate was standing before him, regarding him through a pair of gold-rimmed '''pince-nez''' with a disapproving and hostile expression.}}
#* '''Furst, Alan 2000''' ''Kingdom of Shadows'', p170:
#*: Shabet took a '''pince-nez''' from his breast pocket and settled it on the bridge of his nose.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|Oxford glasses}}

